  "details": "I have encountered a severe memory leak in VRChat that leads to extreme memory usage, eventually causing my system to become unresponsive and sometimes entirely crash. The memory usage can go as far as to begin crashing other apps on my PC, including Windows services, before the game itself crashes. Unfortunately, I have been unable to gather more diagnostic information because my entire system becomes locked up, making it impossible to check performance metrics or logs before a crash occurs.\n\nI have also not been able to consistently reproduce this issue, but I have noticed that it tends to occur in play sessions where I have used the VRChat camera. While I cannot confirm the camera is the cause, it seems to be a common factor in the sessions where I experience the memory leak.\n\nI expect that VRChat should maintain stable memory usage and not progressively consume large amounts of RAM until the system crashes. However, in actuality VRChat's memory usage increases drastically over time, maxxing out available system memory, causing the system to lock up and crash.\n\nThe reproduction rate for this issue is unclear, but happens frequently in sessions where I use the VRChat camera.\n\nSystem Specs:\n\nVRChat Version: 2025.1.1 Build 1568\n\nOperating System: Windows 11 Home 23H2\n\nVR Hardware: Meta Quest 3 via Virtual Desktop\n\nGPU: NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2070\n\nRAM: 32 GB\n\nIf anyone else has encountered this memory leak or has more insight into what might be triggering it, please share your findings!",
